      "lineNbr": 438,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-12T12:07:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. With `NO_VBMETA_PARTITION`. It first tries to read VBMeta directly from the partition `vbmeta`, if failed, it then tries to parse the footer of `boot` to get the VBMeta offset/size and then read it. After that it loads the requested partition with `get_preloaded_partition` to verify. The log is like this:\n\n```\navb_slot_verify.c:731: DEBUG: Loading vbmeta struct from partition \u0027vbmeta\u0027.\navb_slot_verify.c:751: DEBUG: vbmeta: No such partition. Trying \u0027boot\u0027 instead.\navb_slot_verify.c:726: DEBUG: Loading vbmeta struct in footer from partition \u0027boot\u0027.\navb_slot_verify.c:419: DEBUG: initrd_normal: Loading entire partition.\n...\n```",
      "parentUuid": "33d26f5b_a13a31ef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 438,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 438,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "d12aed6b1db02c7cbead781ca8876c11fe24fd18",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
